# Lockstep session (restart, item 5: R030+0x0C44's own Alt-Q case, 0x0CD5..0x100E, tick_keys.py): DKSAVE17 on the map. Right and Alt-Q
# pressed together: the map's look reads Right and then the waiting Alt-Q (R030+0x0540..0x057B), so the map's handler gets Alt-Q: it frees
# the row buffer and the cell buffer (DS:2870, 7E3E:1FFC) and the icon pictures (DS:E416), then exit-to-system asks "Quit to DOS?"
# (root 0000:13A0); N goes on, with the buffers freed; a walk after it. (A second Alt-Q would end the program: local/batch/mapquit.)
key:t
wait:5
key:l
wait:300
state:loaded
tkey:0:right,altq
wait:100
key:n
wait:300
state:no1
click:150,110
wait:600
state:walked
click:250,60
wait:600
state:walked2
